+2. Adding A from its standalone product page redirected to /checkout/; classic cart then contained only A, quantity 1, subtotal $10.
+3. Adding B from its standalone product page redirected to /checkout/ and displayed: “SLT Fixed Three Cycles” has been added to your cart.
+4. The classic cart then contained only B, quantity 1, subtotal $7. A was absent. No authored rejection appeared.
+5. After restoring A alone, block cart and block checkout showed one A line at $10 and no cart error.
+6. Archive search exact text redirected to the product page because it had one result. The broader /?post_type=product&s=SLT archive page 2 exposed B's exact archive add link.
+7. With A in the cart, archive GET /page/2/?post_type=product&s=SLT&slt_cb=202608072001&add-to-cart=11933 redirected to /checkout/ (200). The page displayed the same added-to-cart success notice and the cart contained only B.
+8. After emptying and adding A twice from its product page, the classic cart contained only A at quantity 1/subtotal $10, not quantity 2/subtotal $20.
+9. Cart was emptied through the UI and the exact browser session was closed.
+
+Console: only WooCommerce dependency diagnostics/JQMIGRATE; browser errors: none.
+No order, subscription, user, coupon, product, or setting was created or changed.
